.TH BACAK-GREETER 1 "June 2026" "BDM 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bacak-greeter \- unprivileged login UI for the Bacak Display Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bacak-greeter
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bacak-greeter
is the login screen shown by
.BR bacak-display-manager (8).
It runs fully unprivileged as the
.B bacak-greeter
system user and communicates with the daemon only through the IPC socket named
in the
.B BDM_GREETER_SOCKET
environment variable.
.PP
The greeter presents the user list, accepts a username and secret (relayed to
PAM by the daemon), offers session and power menus, and \(em when a touchscreen
is present \(em an on-screen keyboard. The protocol logic lives in a display
free client core; a reference terminal frontend and a Wayland/iced graphical
frontend share it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BDM_GREETER_SOCKET
Path to the daemon IPC socket. Set by the daemon when it spawns the greeter.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bacak-display-manager (8),
.BR bacak-session-launcher (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Bacak Desktop Project.
